hello there steve here again  today i'm also going to talk about  english common difficulties in english  i'm going to try to speak slowly  and i'm going to talk about verb tenses  now  you may have seen that um  after my video on monday where i spoke  about  i am bored and i am boring and so forth  i also did a video on the same subject  in japanese and had a discussion with  anna in spanish on the same subject  and tomorrow i'm going to do a  portuguese discussion with gabrielle  silva from brazil  we're going to talk about that and other  things  i don't know how useful they are  because i think it's better to listen  for any english learners out there to  listen to me in english  you can  import the youtube video with  closed captions with subtitles into link  as a lesson and work on these issues in  english  so  tenses are a major  difficulty for learners of english  there seem to be a lot of tenses in  english  however i must say that in learning  persian or greek not to mention spanish  and other romance languages they also  have a lot of tenses  so every language  says  you know is able to express the same  ideas and the same nuances but they do  it in different ways  so  with english tenses you have to get a  sense  of the meaning  and get a sense therefore of how certain  things are said you have to get used to  it  now you can read explanations about  tenses but you have to listen to enough  and read enough  in the language  so that  these ways of expressing ideas become  natural to you because they are not  natural in your own language you are  learning a different way of expressing  things but a few comments about  english  tenses first of all  many people struggle with the continuous  form  i am going i was going  i would have been going  so  first bit of advice is if in doubt use  the simple form  if in doubt don't say  i was living say i lived  instead of saying i am eating say i eat  because in many cases both are okay  and it sounds stranger to use  the continuous form  where it's not okay whereas in many  situations if you use the simple form  actually it's quite acceptable so when  in doubt use the simple form  so instead of saying  i was living in france for three years  you just say i lived in france for three  years  i am eating breakfast every day just say  i eat breakfast every day go for the  simple form that's the first bit of  advice okay the next thing is  when you see a phrase which contains  some  form of the verb some tense  that you feel you have trouble with  underline it save it see what other  words are there  so  for example  if it's say every day if you see the  word every day that can't have the  continuous form don't ask me for the  logic  but that's how it is so i eat breakfast  every day we simply don't say i am  eating breakfast every day  logically it's continuous why wouldn't  you say i am eating every day but we  don't say that we say i eat breakfast  every day so that  every day  or always  most of the time  is it means you'll have the simple  present okay  on the other hand if you see  you know  uh i was eating breakfast  when the phone rang  we wouldn't say i ate breakfast when the  phone rang  we might but mostly we would say i was  eating so that when that sort of when  something happened  suggests that it will be continuous  don't ask why i mean you can read all  the explanations of why  it may help you a little bit it's  probably useful thing to do if  particularly if you read the grammar  explanations in english that helps your  english but in the end you have to get  used to  the sort of environment the environment  what are the words that seem to trigger  trigger certain tenses  um  uh you know  and so i i don't want to go into more  examples i want to keep the video short  try  to uh get used to and therefore you have  to grab not just  that tense  but everything that surrounds the tense  and if you're on link  you can save these phrases and you can  tag them and then you can look at them  sort of  in a concentrated form and try to get a  sense  get a sense and we all struggle with  this uh in my russian i struggle with  certain things that are  in the russian language which don't  exist in english i have to develop a new  habit the explanations  are of marginal value i have to be  exposed to so much of the language that  these things start to become  natural i mean if i think of japanese  for example you know  i don't know any grammatical terms in  japanese i really don't  but if i say tabemas tabete mas  tabitemas is some kind of a continuous  form it's just something that i after a  while start to naturally say so  and one other thing i would add is you  have to want to acquire the new habit  you have to want to acquire it i  remember i once read a book called the  mind and the brain and one of the things  they talked about in there was people  who have obsessive compulsive behavior  people who feel they have to wash their  hands every five minutes  these people  who often are given medicine to cure  this compulsive behavior  this psychologist discovered that if he  was able to persuade this person that  there was a circuit there was something  happening in his brain  that didn't have to be him  that he had to want to have to recognize  that he he didn't have to have that  compulsive behavior that that is  something that's happening in his brain  that he can  want just through his his willpower can  want to stop okay now i don't want to  get carried away with the psychological  analysis here but  you have to say i want to develop new  language habits  i have to have these habits in order to  naturally use the language correctly  there is a system in every language and  that system  we can explain it but that doesn't  really do it for us we have to want to  develop these new habits we develop them  best through lots of exposure and using  the language but also because we want to  develop the habits we want to notice how  the language works and we want that to  become a new habit so that's my advice  on tenses and  i don't know if i'm gonna do these all  in different languages maybe it's best  that you take these lessons as an  opportunity to improve your english to  listen to read  and hopefully develop some new habits  bye for now
 

